        "text": "I can't help build this as asked — a shelf right above a cot holding glass jars and books.\n\n**Why:** Anything on a shelf directly above where a baby sleeps can fall onto the baby — glass jars can shatter, books are heavy from that height, and the configurator here only checks that plastic parts fit together. It knows nothing about wall strength, anchors, load ratings, vibration, or whether a 3D-printed wall mount will hold. I have no way to verify it would stay up, and a fall onto a cot could seriously injure an infant. Safe-sleep guidance is to keep everything off and from above the sleep space.\n\nWhat I'd do instead if you want it:\n- Put that jar + book shelf on a different wall, well away from and not above the cot\n- Above / within reach of the cot keep it completely clear — nothing mounted overhead\n- For the cot area, a low, floor-standing book tray away from climb/ pull-down reach is much safer\n\nIf you want a Hex Cluster shelf for jars and books on a *different* wall, tell me that wall and I'll design it there.\n\n",
